.TH ENV 1 "OShell Built-in Commands"
.SH NAME
env \- print all environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B env
command prints all environment variables in the format NAME=VALUE, one per line.
.PP
Environment variables are inherited from the parent process and can be modified using
.BR setenv (1)
and
.BR unsetenv (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B env
Print all environment variables:
.RS
.IP
USER=johndoe
.br
HOME=/home/johndoe
.br
PATH=/bin:/usr/bin
.br
PWD=/home/johndoe
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setenv (1),
.BR unsetenv (1),
.BR bash (1)